  {
   "card": "W03-01",
   "registered_verdict": null,
   "registered_verifier": "qoder-desktop:/root/independent_verifier_w0301d",
   "verdict_files": 4,
   "per_verdict": [
    {
     "file": "independent_review.json",
     "verdict": "REWORK_REQUIRED - the additive migration, the single-transaction mapping shape, the binding command and the evidence chain all verify clean under my own re-runs, but the delivered AdvanceWatermark cannot step the event watermark by one event (P1) and two receipt claims are not supported by what was actually tested (P3, P5). Do not register ACCEPTED for W03-01 on this evidence.",
     "reviewer": "qoder-desktop:/root/independent_verifier_w0301",
     "reservations": 0,
     "limitations": 6,
     "blocking_issues": 0,
     "blocking_ids": []
    },
    {
     "file": "independent_review_rework.json",
     "verdict": "REWORK_AGAIN - all ten first-round items are genuinely closed and I confirmed each one by my own execution, but the rework itself introduced two new defects in this card's own files: (N1) the three contract timestamps the P9 fix added (lease_expires_at, sealed_at, archived_at) are written by MapClientSession as raw *time.Time, so they land in Go's time.String() form ('2026-10-01 16:49:14.8163247 +0000 UTC') instead of RFC3339/date-time and cannot be scanned back as a time, which breaks exactly the WriterLease.expires_at / SessionSnapshot.archived_at contract fields P9 was meant to satisfy, and the shipped check never sets those fields so it cannot see it; (N2) the P10 restore fence can never be satisfied through any production code path - client_session_require_fresh demands a runtime_observations row whose epoch equals the session's own writer_epoch, while the only writer of that table (internal/domain/runtime.go:113) records the Run's lease_epoch, and the helper seeds a barrier for every open session with a run_id regardless of that run's status or even its existence, so after one backup restore a session's handoff is blocked permanently. Do not register ACCEPTED for W03-01 on this evidence.",
     "reviewer": "qoder-desktop:/root/independent_verifier_w0301b",
     "reservations": 0,
     "limitations": 7,
     "blocking_issues": 0,
     "blocking_ids": []
    },
